# 3 readings by claude-opus-5-5, compared
locke-treatise-1.md:1: argue/readings: S3 is read 2 ways: locke-treatise-1.logic.r1 and locke-treatise-1.logic.r1.2 have "end_continuation ∧ ¬end_barely_procreation" and "O parents_sustain_young"; locke-treatise-1.logic.r1.3 has "end_continuation ∧ ¬end_barely_procreation" and "parents_sustain_young"; they differ when only "the end of conjunction between male and female is the continuation of the species" and "it ought to be that the young are sustained by those that got them till they are able to shift and provide for themselves" are true, which the first allows
locke-treatise-1.md:1: argue/modal-ambiguous: S3 is read locke-treatise-1.logic.r1.3 with no modality; locke-treatise-1.logic.r1 and locke-treatise-1.logic.r1.2 as what ought to be or is permitted: the text does not say which it means
locke-treatise-1.md:1: argue/answered: S3: answered yes, which keeps locke-treatise-1.logic.r1 and locke-treatise-1.logic.r1.2, to: Suppose "the end of conjunction between male and female is the continuation of the species", "it ought to be that the young are sustained by those that got them till they are able to shift and provide for themselves" and "it ought to be that the young are sustained by those that got them till they are able to shift and provide for themselves" are true and "the end of conjunction between male and female is barely procreation" and "the young are sustained by those that got them till they are able to shift and provide for themselves" are false. Is S3, "For the end of conjunction, between male and female, being not barely procreation, but the continuation of the species; thisconjunction betwixt male and female ought to last, even after procreation, so long as is necessary to the nourishment and support of the young ones, who are to be sustained by those that got them, till they are able to shift and provide for themselves.", true then?
locke-treatise-1.logic.r1: argue/readings: what the text leaves unstated is read 3 ways: locke-treatise-1.logic.r1 has "end_continuation ∧ O parents_sustain_young → O conj_lasts"; locke-treatise-1.logic.r1.2 has "end_continuation ∧ ¬end_barely_procreation ∧ O parents_sustain_young → O conj_lasts"; they differ when only "the end of conjunction between male and female is the continuation of the species", "the end of conjunction between male and female is barely procreation", "it ought to be that the young are sustained by those that got them till they are able to shift and provide for themselves" and "it ought to be that the young are sustained by those that got them till they are able to shift and provide for themselves" are true, which the second allows; locke-treatise-1.logic.r1.3 has "end_continuation ∧ parents_sustain_young → O conj_lasts"
